The full run passed all gates. At the shipping preset (`easy`, `n=256`), the observed density was 0 valid witnesses in 200,000 uniformly sampled certificate-language candidates. The strongest current baseline, the capped exact subset DP, examined 50,000 subset states and stopped without a witness in 0.08911326713860035 seconds. That runtime is cheap, so I’ll state plainly in the README that cap exhaustion is not evidence of intrinsic hardness.
